<title>UK: UK's Barrasford makes modest AIM debut.</title>
<headline>UK's Barrasford makes modest AIM debut.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British property investment company Barrasford Holdings Plc made an unspectacular start on the first day of trading on the London Stock Exchange's Alternative Investment Market (AIM) on Friday.</p>
<p>The shares, placed at 6p, were quoted at 7p by 1113 GMT.</p>
<p>Barrasford aims to raise 4.02 million stg in its expansion plan for buying more property.</p>
<p>&quot;I think the prices will go up as the company does have a good reputation,&quot; said one analyst who would not be named.</p>
<p>He added that the company expected its properties to be refurbished and so the total asset value was likely to go up as well.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7945</p>
</text>
